      <section class="tour-section">
        <h2>Overview</h2>
        <p>Kizimkazi on Zanzibar's southeast coast is the only place in East Africa where you can see wild bottlenose dolphins in their natural habitat. We only work with operators certified by the Zanzibar Marine Conservation Society.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="tour-section">
        <h2>What to Expect</h2>
        <ul class="expect-list">
      <li>Early morning departure (dolphins most active at dawn, 6–9 AM)</li>
      <li>3–4 hour boat trip to the dolphin hotspot</li>
      <li>Ethical dolphin watching (no feeding, no chasing, minimal engine noise)</li>
      <li>Snorkeling in the lagoon after dolphin viewing</li>
      <li>Fresh fruit and water included</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="tour-section">
        <h2>Duration & Meeting Point</h2>
        <p><strong>Duration:</strong> 3–4 hours (early morning departure)</p>
        <p><strong>Meeting point:</strong> Kizimkazi fishing village, southeast coast (pickup from nearby hotels included)</p>
      </section>
      <section class="tour-section">
        <h2>Important Notes</h2>
        <ul class="notes-list">
      <li>ETHICAL WARNING: Many operators use illegal methods — feeding, chasing, herding. We only book with certified ethical operators.</li>
      <li>Dolphin sightings are NOT guaranteed — it's wildlife, not a show</li>
      <li>Bring your own snorkel gear if possible</li>
      <li>Best period: June–October and December–March</li>
        </ul>
      </section>
      <section class="tour-section">
